<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>driving-risk-metrics evidence report</title>
<style>
:root {
  --ink: #16202c;
  --muted: #5b6b7c;
  --rule: #d9e0e7;
  --page: #ffffff;
  --panel: #f6f8fa;
  --accent: #1f3a5f;
  --warn: #8a5a00;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    --ink: #e6edf3;
    --muted: #9aa7b4;
    --rule: #2d3742;
    --page: #0f141a;
    --panel: #161d25;
    --accent: #7aa7dd;
    --warn: #e3b341;
  }
}
* {
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
html {
  -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
}
body {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0 1.25rem 5rem;
  background: var(--page);
  color: var(--ink);
  font: 16px/1.65 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", "Noto Sans TC",
        "Microsoft JhengHei", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
}
h1, h2, h3 {
  line-height: 1.25;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
}
h1 {
  max-width: 60rem;
  margin: 2.5rem auto 0.5rem;
  font-size: 1.9rem;
}
section {
  max-width: 60rem;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding-top: 2.25rem;
}
section > h2 {
  margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
  border-bottom: 2px solid var(--rule);
  font-size: 1.3rem;
}
section > h3 {
  margin: 1.75rem 0 0.5rem;
  color: var(--accent);
  font-size: 1.05rem;
}
p {
  max-width: 46rem;
  color: var(--muted);
}
section > p:first-of-type {
  margin-top: 0;
}
code {
  font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, "Cascadia Mono", Consolas,
               "Liberation Mono", monospace;
  font-size: 0.86em;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  word-break: break-all;
}
dl {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: max-content minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 0.35rem 1.25rem;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  border-radius: 8px;
  background: var(--panel);
}
dt {
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 0.85rem;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
}
dd {
  margin: 0;
  min-width: 0;
}
.scroll {
  overflow-x: auto;
  margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
}
table {
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
  font-size: 0.9rem;
}
caption {
  padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 0.85rem;
  text-align: left;
}
th, td {
  padding: 0.45rem 0.7rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  text-align: left;
  vertical-align: top;
}
thead th {
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  background: var(--panel);
  border-bottom: 2px solid var(--rule);
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
tbody tr:hover td {
  background: var(--panel);
}
td em {
  color: var(--warn);
  font-style: normal;
  font-size: 0.78rem;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
}
figure {
  margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
}
figcaption {
  margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 0.85rem;
}
#limitations ul {
  max-width: 46rem;
  padding-left: 1.1rem;
  color: var(--muted);
}
#limitations li {
  margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
}
.lede {
  max-width: 60rem;
  margin: 0 auto;
  color: var(--muted);
}
.lede a {
  color: var(--accent);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Safety-aware segmentation evidence</h1>
<p class="lede">
Generated from the committed evidence of
<a href="https://github.com/kuotunyu/driving-risk-metrics">driving-risk-metrics</a>.
Every number below is bound to a verified claim and its artifact.
繁體中文說明在
<a href="https://github.com/kuotunyu/driving-risk-metrics#readme">repository 首頁</a>。
</p>

<section id="provenance">
<h2>What these numbers describe</h2>
<dl>
<dt>Cohort</dt><dd>{{ provenance.cohort }}</dd>
<dt>Evaluated samples</dt><dd>{{ provenance.sample_count }}</dd>
<dt>Seeds per model</dt><dd>{{ provenance.seed_count }}</dd>
<dt>Interval method</dt><dd>{{ provenance.interval_method }}</dd>
<dt>Protocol hash</dt><dd><code>{{ provenance.protocol_hash }}</code></dd>
<dt>Dataset manifest hash</dt><dd><code>{{ provenance.dataset_manifest_hash }}</code></dd>
</dl>
</section>

<section id="claims">
<h2>Verified claims</h2>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Claim</th><th>Evidence type</th><th>Artifact</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for claim in claims %}
<tr>
<td>{{ claim.text }}</td>
<td>{{ claim.evidence_type }}</td>
<td><code>{{ claim.artifact_path }}{{ claim.metric_path }}</code></td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>

<section id="figures">
<h2>Results</h2>
{% for figure in figures %}
<figure>
<figcaption>
{{ figure.name }} on the {{ provenance.cohort }} cohort, {{ provenance.sample_count }} samples,
{{ provenance.seed_count }} seeds per model, intervals from {{ provenance.interval_method }}.
</figcaption>
{{ figure.html | safe }}
</figure>
{% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="runs">
<h2>The runs behind every number</h2>
<p>
Every aggregate on this page is computed from these runs and no others. The
checkpoint digest identifies the exact weights each row was evaluated from.
</p>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Run</th><th>Model</th><th>Seed</th><th>Status</th><th>Final step</th><th>Temperature</th><th>Checkpoint SHA-256</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for run in runs %}
<tr>
<td><code>{{ run.run_id }}</code></td>
<td>{{ run.model }}</td>
<td>{{ run.seed }}</td>
<td>{{ run.status }}</td>
<td>{{ run.final_step }}</td>
<td>{{ run.temperature }}</td>
<td><code>{{ run.checkpoint_sha256 }}</code></td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>

<section id="per-class">
<h2>Per-class scores, with the support they rest on</h2>
<p>
A class is marked <strong>thin</strong> when it appears in fewer than
{{ thin_class_image_count }} images of the cohort. The mark states a count, not a
judgement: a score computed over a handful of images is reported, and how little it
rests on is reported beside it.
</p>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Labelled pixels</th><th>Images</th>{% for model in per_class.models %}<th>{{ model }} IoU</th><th>{{ model }} recall</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for row in per_class.rows %}
<tr>
<td>{{ row.name }}{% if row.thin %} <em>thin</em>{% endif %}</td>
<td>{{ row.support_pixels }}</td>
<td>{{ row.images_with_class }}</td>
{% for score in row.scores %}<td>{{ score.iou }}</td><td>{{ score.recall }}</td>{% endfor %}
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>

<section id="calibration">
<h2>Calibration, pooled and per seed</h2>
<p>
Temperature scaling does not always help. The pooled value is given beside every
seed so that a model whose calibration error rose can be seen to have risen in each
run rather than on average.
</p>
{% for row in calibration %}
<h3>{{ row.model }}</h3>
<p>
Temperature scaling {{ row.direction }} the expected calibration error, from
{{ row.uncalibrated.ece }} to {{ row.calibrated.ece }}; the Brier score moved from
{{ row.uncalibrated.brier }} to {{ row.calibrated.brier }}.
</p>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Seed</th><th>Uncalibrated ECE</th><th>Calibrated ECE</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for seed in row.per_seed %}
<tr><td>{{ seed.seed }}</td><td>{{ seed.uncalibrated_ece }}</td><td>{{ seed.calibrated_ece }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="risk-profiles">
<h2>Risk-weighted cost under each profile</h2>
<p>
A cost-risk figure means nothing without the profile that weighted it, so each is
published beside the class identifiers it treats as critical.
</p>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Profile</th><th>Critical class IDs</th><th>Sensitivity</th><th>Model</th><th>Cost risk</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for profile in risk_profiles %}{% for entry in profile.cost_risk %}
<tr>
<td>{{ profile.name }}</td>
<td>{{ profile.critical_class_ids | join(", ") }}</td>
<td>{{ profile.sensitivity }}</td>
<td>{{ entry.model }}</td>
<td>{{ entry.value }}</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>

<section id="bands">
<h2>Accuracy by normalized image band</h2>
{% if bands.not_computed %}
<p>Not computed: {{ bands.not_computed }}.</p>
{% else %}
<p>{{ bands.definition }}.</p>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Band</th><th>Pixel accuracy</th><th>Pixels</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for row in bands.rows %}{% for band in row.bands %}
<tr><td>{{ row.model }}</td><td>{{ band.band }}</td><td>{{ band.pixel_accuracy }}</td><td>{{ band.pixels }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% endif %}
</section>

<section id="instances">
<h2>Instance coverage, by size and by class</h2>
<p>
Every instance carries equal weight, so a distant pedestrian counts as much as a
nearby bus. Coverage is measured over the footprint that the semantic and instance
annotations corroborate; the mean corroborated fraction below says how much of each
instance that footprint was. An instance is a critical miss when less than half of
its footprint is classified correctly.
</p>
{% if ground_truth.not_computed %}
<p>Ground truth: not computed. {{ ground_truth.not_computed }}.</p>
{% else %}
<p>
Ground truth: {{ ground_truth.masks_verified }} masks verified against the frozen
manifest, over the <code>{{ ground_truth.split_name }}</code> split.
</p>
{% endif %}
{% if instances.not_computed %}
<p>Instance coverage: not computed. {{ instances.not_computed }}.</p>
{% endif %}
{% for row in instances.rows %}
<h3>{{ row.model }}</h3>
<p>
{{ row.instance_count }} instances scored, {{ row.excluded_without_semantic_pixels }}
excluded for having no corroborated pixel, mean corroborated fraction
{{ row.mean_corroborated_fraction }}, tertile edges
<code>{{ row.tertile_edges_sha256 }}</code>.
</p>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Tertile</th><th>Instances</th><th>Critical misses</th><th>Mean correct fraction</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for tertile in row.by_tertile %}
<tr><td><em>all classes</em></td><td>{{ tertile.tertile }}</td><td>{{ tertile.instance_count }}</td><td>{{ tertile.critical_misses }}</td><td>{{ tertile.mean_correct_fraction }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
{% for entry in row.by_class %}{% for tertile in entry.by_tertile %}
<tr><td>{{ entry.class_name }}</td><td>{{ tertile.tertile }}</td><td>{{ tertile.instance_count }}</td><td>{{ tertile.critical_misses }}</td><td>{{ tertile.mean_correct_fraction }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="selective-risk">
<h2>Selective risk</h2>
<p>
Each curve is evaluated at confidence-bin boundaries rather than continuously, so
the area below is the area under a quantized curve. It is comparable across the
models on this page and not with a figure computed another way.
</p>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Uncalibrated AURC</th><th>Calibrated AURC</th><th>Coverage points</th><th>Defined at</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for row in selective_risk %}
<tr>
<td>{{ row.model }}</td>
<td>{{ row.uncalibrated.aurc }}</td>
<td>{{ row.calibrated.aurc }}</td>
<td>{{ row.uncalibrated.coverage_points }} / {{ row.calibrated.coverage_points }}</td>
<td><code>{{ row.calibrated.defined_at }}</code></td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>

<section id="gallery">
<h2>Best and worst samples</h2>
<p>
Selected by {{ gallery.rule.metric }} aggregated as {{ gallery.rule.aggregate }} over
the <code>{{ gallery.evaluation }}</code> pass, {{ gallery.rule.per_model }} per model
per end, ties broken by {{ gallery.rule.tie_break }}. This release redistributes no
dataset images, so the samples are named rather than shown.
</p>
{% for row in gallery.rows %}
<h3>{{ row.model }}</h3>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
<thead><tr><th>End</th><th>Sample ID</th><th>Mean IoU over seeds</th>{% for seed in row.seeds %}<th>seed {{ seed }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for entry in row.best %}
<tr><td>best</td><td><code>{{ entry.sample_id }}</code></td><td>{{ entry.mean_iou_over_seeds }}</td>{% for seed in row.seeds %}<td>{{ entry.per_seed[seed] }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% endfor %}
{% for entry in row.worst %}
<tr><td>worst</td><td><code>{{ entry.sample_id }}</code></td><td>{{ entry.mean_iou_over_seeds }}</td>{% for seed in row.seeds %}<td>{{ entry.per_seed[seed] }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="rankings">
<h2>Ranking comparison</h2>
<p>
Each safety metric below is compared against the baseline metric
<code>{{ rankings.baseline_metric }}</code>. A reversal is an observation about this
cohort, not a success criterion.
</p>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Baseline order</th><th>Comparison order</th><th>Reversal observed</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for comparison in rankings.comparisons %}
<tr>
<td>{{ comparison.metric_name }}</td>
<td>{{ comparison.baseline_order | join(", ") }}</td>
<td>{{ comparison.comparison_order | join(", ") }}</td>
<td>{{ comparison.reversal_observed }}</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>

<section id="limitations">
<h2>Limitations</h2>
<ul>
{% for limitation in limitations %}
<li>{{ limitation }}</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
</section>
</body>
</html>
